{{wikipedia|Phantasmagoria}}
==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[phantasmagory]]
* [[fantasmagoria]]

===Etymology===
From Greek φαντασμα phantasma (ghost) + αγορευειν agoreuein (to speak publicly)

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˌfæntæzməˈgɒriə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌfæntæzməˈgɔːriə/}}
* {{audio|en-us-phantasmagoria.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ɔːriə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A series of events involving rapid changes in light intensity and colour.
# A dreamlike state where real and imagined elements are blurred together.

====Derived terms====
* [[phantasmagoric]]
* [[phantasmagorical]]
* [[phantasmagorically]]

